; The Seatbelt profile of cove-vmm. Everything is denied, then allowed only what libkrun was seen
; to be refused while it booted a VM: the rules were found from the denials the kernel logs
; (log show --predicate 'eventMessage CONTAINS "cove-vmm-krun("'), one at a time.
(version 1)
(deny default)

; The files of the VM are allowed after these rules, each by its exact path, as Enter writes
; them: reading for the kernel, the initramfs and the layers, writing as well for the write disk
; and the console, binding for the sockets the host reaches the guest by. Nothing else is: not
; their directory, not another file of it, not a link.

; Hypervisor.framework asks whether it runs in a VM itself, and libkrun sizes the memory of the
; guest in pages of the host.
(allow sysctl-read (sysctl-name "kern.hv_vmm_present" "hw.pagesize_compat"))
